# beacond runtime directories. dh_installtmpfiles installs this to
# /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/beacond.conf and invokes systemd-tmpfiles from the
# postinst -- after systemd-sysusers (see debian/rules), so the beacon user
# already exists when these paths are chowned to it.
#
# /var/lib/beacond is the beacon user's $HOME (see debian/beacond.sysusers);
# beacond does not currently write there, but the directory must exist to
# match the passwd entry. /var/log/beacond holds rotated log archives (the
# daemon logs to stderr/the journal directly; see README.md).
#Type Path              Mode UID    GID    Age Argument
d     /var/lib/beacond  0750 beacon beacon -
d     /var/log/beacond  0750 beacon beacon -
